# DIE v2.0 - line-ending policy (added while fixing CI regression-harness
# failures, 2026-11-16). The regression baseline (scripts/
# regression_baseline.json) checksums shipped data files byte-for-byte; a
# Windows worktree checked out with core.autocrlf=true differs byte-wise from
# the same content on Linux (CRLF vs LF), which broke the ubuntu CI run.
# Forcing LF for all text files makes every platform's checkout
# byte-identical, so checksums are stable. Binary formats are marked binary
# explicitly (git would auto-detect them, but be explicit for safety).
* text=auto eol=lf
*.parquet binary
*.pmtiles binary
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.nc binary
